<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 4 · Paper B · Learner paper</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-4/b/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 4 Course Review · Original Paper B</p><h1>Learner paper</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 100-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 4 B</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 30 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">食谱: recipe</p><p class="gloss">秤: weighing scale</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. Which practice does the speaker explicitly keep?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只允许使用精确的克数</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先闻香味，再决定是否加料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 取消所有给初学者的说明</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">配菜: vegetable accompaniment</p><p class="gloss">版本: version</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What experience does the man explicitly remember?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 父亲从未更换任何一种材料</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 妹妹独自经营一家面馆</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 家人围着桌子共同准备食物</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why will he describe the changes in the recipe?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 说明做法如何随生活条件延续</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 证明家人从未遇到材料变化</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 让所有读者只照妹妹的版本做</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">采购: purchase supplies</p><p class="gloss">结算: settle costs</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What is the first school’s stated responsibility?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 集中购买后按实际用量结算</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 替所有小组承担全部费用</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 不提供任何数量和费用信息</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What caused the misunderstanding?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 两校对纸张颜色有不同喜好</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 采购方临时取消了全部材料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把统一提供误解为免费承担费用</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">注明: state explicitly</p><p class="gloss">清单: list</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What must each group submit before Monday noon?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 注明收件代表的材料清单</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 越长越好的临时项目建议</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已经完成的全部工作坊作品</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">占用: occupied</p><p class="gloss">状态: status</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What useful role do both reports recognize?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 保证显示有空就一定订好了</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 让工作人员不必知道最终状态</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 帮助查看空位或减少协调时间</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which change addresses both users’ needs?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 提交显示确认结果，取消也同步更新</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只显示空闲颜色，不反馈提交与取消</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 取消后只让用户在聊天群留言</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">管理员: room supervisor</p><p class="gloss">试行: pilot arrangement</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Which rule is explicitly included in the proposed arrangement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 所有时段之间都取消整理时间</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每段使用之间留十分钟整理</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每组只需付钱，不必整理桌椅</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. Why does the man support the adjustment with a condition?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 已经确认预约越密管理员越轻松</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 希望所有小组改成整晚包场</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 增加短时机会时也要顾及整理负担</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">合唱: choir</p><p class="gloss">乐谱: musical score</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the programme’s main purpose?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 考试听众识读乐谱的能力</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 用例子讨论同一活动的不同感受</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 选出最懂音乐的唯一讲述者</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">合唱团: choir</p><p class="gloss">时机: timing</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How do the two recording segments show a change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从参加合唱变成拒绝开口</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从抢先唱到听别人后同步结束</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 证明第二段的每个人都唱得更响</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which attitude best fits the editor’s explanation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要声音变小，就必定失去信心</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 任何别的录音都一定表达相同变化</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 用具体声音线索判断，不把音量等同于信心</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">水龙头: tap</p><p class="gloss">总量: total volume</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What concrete action does Report A describe?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只换宣传口号，不处理漏水</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已经测量并证明全校效果相同</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 修好漏水处后记录同一教室用水</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which comparison is justified by both reports?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 把所有减少都归功于口号并推广全校</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 连同人数和课程记录，限定结论范围</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只比较两周总量，忽略教学活动差异</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">7:30 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">数据: data</p><p class="gloss">更正: correct</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. Which condition limits the revised report?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 所有没记录的日子都算完全不用水</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只记录一间教室，缺少的日期不填零</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 另一间教室已证明效果完全相同</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">预约屏: booking kiosk</p><p class="gloss">确认按钮: confirmation button</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What helps explain the different experiences?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 所有使用者都已独立完成全部步骤</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 文字可读性和对确认步骤的理解不同</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 放大后的页面已经通过所有人测试</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. Which claim exceeds the interviews’ evidence?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 保留工作人员帮助可能有必要</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 放大文字后还需检查按钮是否可见</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 各年龄所有人已经无需帮助都会使用</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">兼顾: consider both needs</p><p class="gloss">无从下手: not know where to start</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. How did the organizers reconcile the two needs?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 保留经验叙述，再共同试做并补参考用量</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 删除老人的全部经验，只发统一数字</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 禁止初学者询问怎样判断味道</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. How has the speaker’s view of preserving a recipe changed?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从记录数字扩展到理解经验来源与受众需要</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 认为用量只要改变就必定失去传统</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 决定把一位老人的做法当所有人的标准</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">家庭食谱册决定保留讲述者自己给菜起的名字。编辑发现，同一道菜在不同家庭有不同称呼，直接统一名字虽然方便目录排序，却可能让讲述者认不出自己的经历。于是每页先印本人选定的名字，再补一个便于查找的通用类别。类别只作索引，不表示哪种叫法更正确。编辑还会写明这些记录来自自愿参加的家庭，不能把册子当成所有地区饮食习惯的完整说明。</p></div><p class="gloss">索引: index</p><p class="gloss">类别: category</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. What will each recipe page explicitly retain?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 讲述者自己选定的菜名</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有家庭必须使用的同一菜名</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 取消来源的通用饮食标准</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小溪准备把母亲常做的汤写进家庭食谱册。母亲说，这种汤以前需要长时间慢煮，她当年有空照顾炉火，所以不觉得麻烦。现在小溪放学后常要参加活动，回家较晚，便试着把部分材料提前处理。她在记录里说明，这次调整是为了配合自己的时间，不能反过来说母亲原来的办法不好。<br>试做时，她发现提前处理以后，有一种材料放久了味道会变，于是保留那一步到最后才做。母亲也同意在原方法旁边加入这个版本，并写上适用条件。小溪原先想把步骤改得越少越好，后来认识到，改写食谱不只是删去麻烦，还需要理解原步骤的作用。册子会让两种方法并列，读者按自己的条件选择，不把家庭经验写成人人都必须遵守的规则。</p></div><p class="gloss">炉火: cooking heat</p><p class="gloss">适用条件: conditions of use</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What reason does Xiaoxi explicitly give for adjusting the method?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 证明母亲原来的全部步骤有害</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 要求所有读者都取消最后一步</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 配合放学活动后的时间安排</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why are the two methods displayed together?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 证明步骤越少在所有情况下越好</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把一次试做的结果变成所有家庭规则</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 说明不同条件下的选择及原步骤作用</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，联合活动通知：两校会在各自网站介绍周六工作坊，欢迎同学了解。网站发布介绍不等于替学生完成报名，参加者仍须填写统一表格，并等候确认。人数满后可以登记候补，未收到确认者不要先购买指定材料。各校代表只负责转发信息。<br>材料乙，代表来信：我看到本校已经宣传，就以为报名也由学校统一办好，告诉同学直接来。现在有人问为什么名单没有他们，我才发现自己把发布介绍和确认参加混在一起。我会马上更正，附上统一表格，并询问尚有多少位置。对已买材料的人，我只能说明情况并请负责人协助，不能擅自承诺他们一定能进场。</p></div><p class="gloss">候补: waiting list</p><p class="gloss">擅自: without authorization</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. What does the notice explicitly require from participants?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 填统一表格并等候确认</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 看到宣传后直接到场即可</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先买材料就自动取得名额</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. Which misunderstanding must be clarified?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 材料价格已经被学校全面免除</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 学校转发介绍不等于学生已确认参加</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 主办方已承诺所有人不限人数入场</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">跨校工作坊的准备表要求，每组周二前确认要使用的语言和需要解释的关键词。两种语言并用的组可以缩短每次发言，不必把整段内容逐句重复。组织者会提供时间表，但不会替小组判断哪些表达最适合自己的听众。各组需先问伙伴希望了解什么，再选材料。若仍有意见不同，应把问题写给两校代表共同确认，不能只把本校讨论的结果当成双方已经同意。</p></div><p class="gloss">关键词: key terms</p><p class="gloss">逐句: sentence by sentence</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What must groups confirm before Tuesday?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 所有人都必须逐句重复两遍</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 本校决定自动代表双方意见</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 使用语言及需解释的关键词</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，试用说明：共享预约日历可以显示活动室哪些时段已被占用，帮助其他小组选择时间。普通使用者只需看到时段和状态，管理人员才能查看联系人。试用组认为，公开每位预约者的全部姓名和联系方式并不是查找空位所必需的。提交后，预约者会收到确认编号。<br>材料乙，用户建议：我支持让大家知道房间是否有空，但不愿为了预约把私人联系方式公布给所有人。上次朋友只能通过一张截屏转发取消消息，也不知道管理人员是否收到。我希望可以用确认编号查询和取消自己的预约，同时让管理人员有办法联系我。对其他小组显示最终空位就够了，不必把个人资料一起放在公共页面上。</p></div><p class="gloss">确认编号: confirmation reference</p><p class="gloss">联系人: contact person</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. What shared purpose do the explanation and suggestion support?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 向所有人公布完整私人联系方式</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 用截屏代替所有正式取消操作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 显示可用时段以帮助安排活动</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which design meets both texts’ requirements?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 公开时段状态，凭编号管自己的预约，联系人限管理端</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 公开全部联系人，取消只靠朋友转发截屏</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 隐藏所有空位，也不向本人反馈确认</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">社区活动室准备试行半小时预约，满足只需短时见面的读书小组。每次结束后保留十分钟，由使用者把桌椅归位并交还钥匙。晚上八点以后只有一位管理员，他不能同时整理房间和替下一组开门，因此确认消息里会写明交接要求。需要移动大件家具的活动本周暂不接受。<br>一位小组代表认为，新安排能增加短时使用机会，但必须看实际交接是否顺利。如果每组都迟十分钟离开，后面的时段再多也没有意义。他建议试行时分别记录预约时间、实际交接时间和未完成的整理项目，再听管理员及使用者的意见。支持半小时安排，并不表示每个活动都适合缩短到半小时，也不表示应该把所有间隔取消。</p></div><p class="gloss">交接: handover</p><p class="gloss">归位: restore to position</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. Which restriction is explicitly stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 所有活动一律必须缩到半小时</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 八点以后由两位管理员负责整理</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本周暂不接受需移动大件家具的活动</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. What limits the representative’s support?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 预约数量一多就已证明所有人受益</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只问使用者，不必了解管理员负担</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 短时机会需以可行交接和实际记录为依据</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原创声音节目《第一次合唱》把三位虚构同学的回忆放在同一段排练声音旁边。节目介绍请普通听众注意，每个人选择的细节是否支持他说的感受。有的人听见节奏变齐，有的人注意到自己不再害怕开口。组织者不要求听众懂专业乐理，也没有宣布某一位同学的经历才最真实。讨论时可以比较不同叙述，但应区分录音里确实听到的内容与自己补出的猜想，并说明判断依据。</p></div><p class="gloss">乐理: music theory</p><p class="gloss">节奏: rhythm</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What are ordinary listeners invited to do?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只听专业人士宣布哪个经历最真实</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 根据录音细节比较不同感受和判断依据</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 在没有依据时补出所有人物的想法</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原创短故事：音频社团要为新成员录一段欢迎词。小原把自己的长介绍交给同伴，却发现最后成品只留下三句。他先以为别人不重视自己，准备退出录制。后来同伴拿出时间表，解释每个人只有半分钟，长稿里的例子并未被删掉，而是放进节目后的文字页。小原听完，主动问能否把最重要的一句放在结尾。<br>读书小组的评论认为，小原从猜测他人态度转向询问安排，是故事里值得注意的变化。成品缩短这件事本身不能证明谁受到轻视；需要结合半分钟限制和文字页的安排理解。评论没有说所有删稿都合理，也没有断定小原从此不会误会别人。其他读者可以质疑这次分配是否公平，但应指出故事中可讨论的细节，而不是替人物写出没有出现的动机。</p></div><p class="gloss">成品: finished recording</p><p class="gloss">轻视: disrespect</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Which details explain why the recording was shortened?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 同伴承认不重视小原并删除全部例子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每人半分钟，较长例子另放文字页</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 小原已经退出，完全拒绝参与</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which inference respects the story’s limits?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 这次他开始询问安排，但不能推断以后永不误会</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有被缩短的介绍都必然受到公平对待</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 同伴必定一直想让小原退出社团</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，菜园用水方案：同学准备在午休后按固定时间给三块菜地浇水，便于安排值日。方案要求每组记录浇水前泥土是否仍湿，若已经足够湿就先暂停，并写明原因。固定时间是提醒，不表示每天都必须用相同水量。工作人员周五会检查记录。<br>材料乙，课堂补充：本周二下过雨，周三两组都发现泥土仍湿，因此没有继续浇水；周四较热，一块靠墙菜地较快变干。老师请大家把天气和菜地位置与浇水记录一起写下。比较不同组用量时，不要只以谁少谁好判断，因为照顾的条件可能不同。如果记录只写总量、不说明暂停原因，其他同学也难以接替值日。</p></div><p class="gloss">泥土: soil</p><p class="gloss">接替: take over</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. What does the plan explicitly require before watering?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天不看情况使用完全相同水量</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 记录泥土是否仍湿，必要时暂停</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把所有检查都推迟到月底以后</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which comparison is supported by both sources?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一律把用水最少的小组评为最好</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 为方便接替，只记总量不说明原因</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 结合天气位置和暂停理由理解用量差异</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">菜园记录表本周增加一栏，填写没有浇水的原因。若泥土已湿，应写“检查后暂停”；若值日组忘记检查，则写“未检查”，不能把两种情况都记成节约用水。某天缺少记录，也不能补一个零当成确实没有使用。老师说明，这张表用于理解三块菜地的照护情况，还不能说明整个校园的用水变化。下周会先训练大家把观察与行动分开写清，再考虑是否扩大记录范围。</p></div><p class="gloss">照护: care</p><p class="gloss">未检查: not checked</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which distinction does the notice require?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 检查后暂停、未检查与缺记录须分别记录</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 没有记录的日期都自动补成零</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 三块菜地已代表整个校园用水</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，预约工具更新说明：新页面可放大文字，并把确认按钮保留在固定区域。使用者选择课程后仍须检查日期，再按确认；看到课程名称不表示已经预约。语音朗读目前只支持课程介绍，尚未覆盖取消与修改步骤。更新组会继续收集不同设备的反馈。<br>材料乙，用户记录：我把文字放大后，确实更容易看清日期，也能找到确认按钮。但用语音朗读时，修改页面上有两个按钮只读成“按钮”，没有说明各自作用，我请管理员帮忙才完成。我的记录来自一台旧手机的一次使用，不能证明所有设备都有同样问题，也不能因为介绍能朗读就宣称整个预约过程已经完全可用。应先把缺少的名称补好，再让更多使用者测试。</p></div><p class="gloss">语音朗读: spoken screen reading</p><p class="gloss">覆盖: cover/support</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What explains the difference between improved reading and remaining difficulty?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 放大改善日期阅读，但修改步骤仍缺清楚名称</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要介绍可朗读，修改取消就已全部可用</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 使用者没有找到任何日期与确认按钮</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Which claim exceeds the supplied evidence?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 补齐修改按钮名称后仍需要更多测试</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有设备上的整个预约流程已完全可用</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 这位使用者在旧手机上曾需要帮助</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C4B-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">社区家庭食谱工作坊最初要求每位参加者把自己的经验填成统一克数表。一位老人说，家里的办法靠观察颜色和香味，无法直接说出每样几克；初学者却担心没有参考量，回家难以再做。组织者保留共用记录页，让老人先演示判断过程，再由愿意参加的人一起试做，补充大约用量与适用条件。每段说明写清提供经验的人，并交本人确认。<br>后来，有人建议把试做后的用量宣布为社区统一标准。负责同学没有接受，因为不同厨房和份量仍可能需要调整。他在总结里说，记录可以帮助人们分享，却不能把一次合作的结果变成所有家庭的规定。以前他以为传承只要把老方法照写下来，现在更重视把方法的来由讲清，也听见新学习者遇到的困难。留下变化的理由，同样是理解经验的一部分。</p></div><p class="gloss">克数: gram measurements</p><p class="gloss">份量: portion size</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. How did the organizers respond to both needs?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 保留演示经验，共同试做并补参考条件</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 强迫老人把无法确定的数字填成精确值</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只允许初学者看表，不许观察过程</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. Which reflection is supported by the workshop experience?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 合作记录一完成便能规定所有家庭做法</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 分享方法需解释来由和变化，并顾及学习者条件</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只要新学习者有困难就必须删除旧经验</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 30 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 30 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Correct a cross-school plan</h2><p>Reply in Chinese to Lin. Say whether you can join Tuesday lunchtime and whether your group prefers live demonstrations or prerecorded clips. Explain your preference, revise the plan for the new connection limit, and ask a relevant confirmation. Invented details are accepted. About 80–120 Chinese characters is guidance.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小文：周二午休两校要确认工作坊，你能参加吗？你们更想现场演示，还是提前录好短片？我上次说大家可以同时连线，现在才知道另一校只有一台可用设备，不能让每组各开一个房间。请想一个可行调整，也告诉我还需确认什么。我会更正先前的通知。小林</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can join Tuesday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose a format.</li><li>State a clear preference.</li><li>Give a partner-related reason.</li><li>Adjust for one remote device and no simultaneous rooms.</li><li>Ask a relevant confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>Choose a community service proposal</h2><p>Write connected Chinese paragraphs for the community committee. Use at least one accurately attributed detail from EACH proposal. Compare a benefit and a limitation, give a conditional recommendation and a feasible next step. Do not search outside sources. About 180–240 Chinese characters is guidance.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">材料甲，上门送书：两位志愿者周六上午把预订的书送到附近居民门口，适合不方便出门的人；每人每次最多送五户，不能进入住户家中。居民须提前说明要借的书，临时更换较难安排。<br>材料乙，门口流动书桌：在社区中心门口摆两小时，居民可当场翻看和选择，不用预订；下雨时场地不能用，需要提前确认室内替代地点。中心仍只有这两位志愿者，希望照顾不同居民，也不想承诺超出人手的服务。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Identify the service need.</li><li>Use one accurately attributed detail from each proposal.</li><li>Compare a benefit and a limitation.</li><li>Make a conditional recommendation.</li><li>Give a feasible next step.</li><li>Organize connected paragraphs rather than copying.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Negotiate a joint workshop</h2><p>Respond to four fixed prompts about a joint workshop. Each file contains two plays; play once, prepare 15 seconds, respond up to 30 seconds. Explain an audience need, compare formats, respond to a restriction and set a conditional next step. Four responses form ONE /8 task. The recording does not adapt to your answers.</p><p>You and a partner are organizing a joint workshop for learners with different experience. All personal details may be fictional.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Relate your position to an audience need.</li><li>Compare two formats with reasons.</li><li>Revise for a new restriction.</li><li>Explain a compromise and confirm the next step.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Compare school technology support</h2><p>Recommend a support plan to the school. Compare BOTH plans, use at least two details covering both, explain a trade-off and a condition, then give a feasible next step. Either choice can earn full credit. Prepare 60 seconds; speak up to 120 seconds.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">学校情况：三十位新同学要学习预约课程，经验不同；本周只有两位学生助教，周五必须完成入门。<br>甲，集中示范：周三午休一次展示全部步骤，不收费，可同时观看；现场只有一台练习设备，不能保证每个人亲手试。<br>乙，小组练习：每组五人，每次二十分钟，周四和周五午休共能安排四组；每人能尝试，助教可纠正错误；还有十人需要另找练习机会。<br>学校可提前发文字步骤，但不能增加助教或额外午休时段。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare both plans accurately.</li><li>Use at least two details covering both plans.</li><li>Explain a trade-off and condition.</li><li>Propose a feasible next step for this audience.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>